"""T4 adapter for the PDM-Closed reference.

The scorer does not use a trajectory-closeness target for ``EP``. The
reference denominator is produced by the PDM-Closed prior and is then
used by :class:`PDMScorer` when the oracle labels are built.  T4 has the same
ingredients, but not nuPlan's map API or track tokens, so this module provides
the narrow adapter at that boundary:

* T4 route rows become the ordered :class:`PDMPath` and its +/-1 m lateral
  alternatives;
* the original five IDM policies, PDM generator, LQR/bicycle simulator, and
  PDM scorer are used without replacing them with a proxy;
* T4 boxes are associated across frames so PDM collision de-duplication sees
  one object token over time;
* the selected PDM-Closed proposal is scored against the complete T4 future
  observation and its ``raw_progress * NC * DAC`` is stored as ``pdm_progress``.

This code is intentionally CPU/offline.  It is run once by
``build_t4_pdm_reference_cache.py``; training only memory-maps the resulting
labels.  Keeping the expensive geometry here prevents every GPU training step
from rebuilding a closed-loop oracle and, more importantly, makes the oracle
auditable independently of the learned model.
"""

